description:
Trigger Unity script recompilation and wait for it to complete. Unity's auto domain reload is disabled by default — after modifying .cs files you MUST call this once to apply your code changes, always before relying on them in unity_execute. The result reports a stable `status` (`compiled`, `already_converged`, `up_to_date`, `reloaded_without_compile`, `compiled_bridge_recovering`, `existing_reload_incomplete`, `reload_only_incomplete`, `reload_only_bridge_recovering`, or `failed`) together with the relevant compilation, detection, domain reload, bridge, editor, phase, and recommended action fields, so treat those fields as authoritative before choosing the next Unity tool. `already_converged` means a compile already in progress applied the changes; `up_to_date` means Unity's incremental build graph found every assembly current; `reloaded_without_compile` means assemblies were current and a domain reload removed live hot-patch detours.

{optional_capability_guidance}

This tool brings the Unity Editor to the foreground and may take 10-60 seconds depending on project size. Do NOT call it while `editor_status` is `playing` or `playing_paused`.
